oss":"you reject"},{"surface":"ஆயினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"ஆயின்","gloss":"even if"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"even if"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"அளந்து","parts":[{"text":"அள","lemma":"அள","gloss":"measure"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ந்து","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having measured"},{"surface":"அறிவை","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"அறி","gloss":"know"},{"text":"வை","lemma":"வை","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you know"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புரைமை","parts":[{"text":"புரை","lemma":"புரை","gloss":"nobility"},{"text":"மை","lemma":"மை","gloss":"ness"}],"gloss":"nobility"},{"surface":"வாய்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"truth"}],"gloss":"truth"},{"surface":"போல்","parts":[{"text":"போல்","lemma":"போல்","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொய்ம்மொழி","parts":[{"text":"பொய்ம்மொழி","lemma":"பொய்ம்மொழி","gloss":"false words"}],"gloss":"false words","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கூறல்","parts":[{"text":"கூறு","lemma":"கூறு","gloss":"speak"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"speaking"},{"surface":"அஃது","parts":[{"text":"அஃது","lemma":"அஃது","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"எவனோ","parts":[{"text":"எவன்","lemma":"எவன்","gloss":"what/why"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"question particle"}],"gloss":"why?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெஞ்சம்","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சம்","lemma":"நெஞ்சம்","gloss":"heart"}],"gloss":"heart"},{"surface":"நன்றே","parts":[{"text":"நன்று","lemma":"நன்று","gloss":"good"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"is good indeed"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வயினானே","parts":[{"text":"வயின்","lemma":"வயின்","gloss":"place/side"},{"text":"ஆன்","lemma":"ஆன்","gloss":"locative suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"towards you"}]}],"literal":"Rain having reached rising-up rainy-season hill's / waterfall filled-with cool fragrant gloriosa-lily / bud having-blossomed unceasingly sweet-smelling fragrant forehead, / many-petaled cool-eyes dark-skinned-one! / Whether you accept or whether you reject, / you having-measured know. Your nobility truth like / false words speaking, that why? / Heart is good indeed towards you.","translation":"O dark-skinned girl with many-petaled cool eyes, and a fragrant forehead that unceasingly smells of the newly blossomed buds of the cool, sweet gloriosa lilies fed by the waterfalls of the rainy-season hills where clouds gather! Whether you accept us or reject us, you know your own mind. Why then do you speak false words that seem like the truth, contrary to your noble nature? Yet, my heart remains good and devoted only to you.","modern":"மேகங்கள் கூடி எழுகின்ற மழைக்காலத்து மலையின் அருவியால் நனைந்த குளிர்ந்த, நறுமணமுள்ள செங்காந்தள் மொட்டுகள் அவிழ்ந்து இடைவிடாது வீசும் நறுமணம் கமழும் நெற்றியையும், பல இதழ்களைக் கொண்ட குளிர்ந்த கண்களையும் உடைய மாநிறத்து பெண்ணே! நீ எங்களை ஏற்றுக்கொண்டாலும் சரி, எங்களை அழித்தாலும் சரி, அதை நீயே ஆராய்ந்து அறிவாய். உன்னுடைய பெருமைக்குரிய உண்மை போன்ற பொய் மொழிகளைக் கூறுவது ஏனோ? என் நெஞ்சம் எப்போதும் உன்னிடத்தேதான் நன்மையாக இருக்கிறது.","explanation":"This poem is set in the Kuriñci (mountainous) landscape, where the theme is union and the obstacles to it. The speaker is the heroine's friend (tōḻi), addressing the heroine on behalf of the hero, or perhaps the hero himself addressing the heroine. The friend describes the heroine's beauty, comparing her fragrant forehead to the gloriosa lily (kāntal) blooming on the rain-swept hills. This vivid imagery of the Kuriñci landscape—clouds, rain, waterfalls, and blooming lilies—symbolizes the rich, fertile state of their love. She points out that whether the heroine accepts the hero's love ('olvai') or rejects/kills him ('kolvai'), she must decide with her own noble mind. She questions why the heroine speaks evasive or false words ('poymmoḻi') that sound like truth, when the hero's heart is entirely devoted to her.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}